<title>USA: Boeing disappointed with European stance on merger.</title>
<headline>Boeing disappointed with European stance on merger.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co. said Wednesday it was disappointed that an advisory committee to European Union regulators has recommended that its proposed $14 billion merger with McDonnell Douglas Corp. be oppossed.</p>
<p>Boeing said it had failed to reach agreement with the European competition regulators on two major points, its controversial sole supplier agreements with three major U.S. airlines and the merger of Boeing and McDonnell's commercial airplane businesses.</p>
</text>
